Indiana Jones, played by Harrison Ford.

12
00:50:48,000 --> 00:50:54,000
Professor Henry Jones, played by Sean Connery.

13
00:55:02,000 --> 00:55:08,000
Marcus Brody, played by Denholm Elliott.

14
00:59:16,000 --> 00:59:22,000
Elsa, played by Alison Doody.

15
01:03:30,000 --> 01:03:36,000
Sallah, played by John Rhys-Davies.

16
01:07:44,000 --> 01:07:50,000
Walter Donovan, played by Julian Glover.

17
01:11:58,000 --> 01:12:04,000
Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade is a 1989 American action-adventure film directed by Steven Spielberg
from a screenplay by Jeffrey Boam, based on a story by George Lucas and Menno Meyjes.

18
01:16:12,000 --> 01:16:18,000
It is the third installment in the Indiana Jones film series and the
narrative sequel to Raiders of the Lost Ark (1981).

19
01:20:26,000 --> 01:20:32,000
Harrison Ford reprises his role as the titular character,
while Sean Connery co-stars as his father.

20
01:24:40,000 --> 01:24:46,000
Other cast members featured include Alison Doody, Denholm Elliott,
Julian Glover, River Phoenix and John Rhys-Davies.

21
01:28:54,000 --> 01:29:00,000
In the film, set in 1938, Indiana Jones searches for his father, a Holy Grail scholar, who has been
kidnapped and held hostage by the Nazis while on a journey to find the Holy Grail.

22
01:33:08,000 --> 01:33:14,000
After the criticism that Indiana Jones and the Temple of Doom (1984) received, Spielberg chose to make a more
lighthearted film for the next installment, as well as bringing back several elements from Raiders of the Lost Ark.

23
01:37:22,000 --> 01:37:28,000
During the five years between Temple of Doom and The Last Crusade, he and executive
producer Lucas reviewed several scripts before accepting Jeffrey Boam's.

24
01:41:36,000 --> 01:41:42,000
Filming locations included Spain, Italy, West Germany,
Jordan, the United Kingdom, and the United States.

25
01:45:50,000 --> 01:45:56,000
Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade was released in the United
States on May 24, 1989, by Paramount Pictures.

26
01:50:04,000 --> 01:50:10,000
The film received positive reviews and was a financial success, earning $474.2
million worldwide, making it the highest-grossing film of 1989.

27
01:54:18,000 --> 01:54:24,000
It also won the Academy Award for Best Sound Effects Editing and was nominated
for Best Original Score and Best Sound at the 62nd Academy Awards.

28
01:58:32,000 --> 01:58:38,000
Although Spielberg and Lucas originally intended for The Last Crusade to be the end of the series, a sequel, Indiana Jones and the Kingdom of the
Crystal Skull, followed in May 2008, while a fifth and final film, Indiana Jones and the Dial of Destiny, was released in June 2023.

29
02:02:46,000 --> 02:02:52,000
The film explores themes of saving the world, nazi,
holy grail, venice, italy, entrapment.
